x=next(x for x in decomp['records'] if (x['mode'],x['gate'],x['policy'])==('frozen','native_complete','own_selected'))['gap_change_decomposition'];text += [f"**Exact descriptive decomposition:** of the+{x['change']:.4f} own-selected gap shift, {x['construction_composition']:.4f} comes from changed active/passive weights using full-panel construction means as reference, and {x['within_construction_selection']:.4f} from selection within constructions. The split depends on that stated reference; it is arithmetic about the report, not a causal mediation decomposition of model processing.",'', '**Annotation uncertainty matters.** Both checkpoints\' one inseparable unit belongs to c15 (*accompany*), flagged for reciprocity ambiguity during collection before outcomes were inspected. This is weak evidence for a linguistic discrimination deficit. All24 families remain in the primary test; omitting c15 only as a labeled descriptive sensitivity leaves the gap shift+.5321, and omitting both c09/c15 leaves+.5168. No additional p values or relabeling were introduced.','', f"**Endpoint/storage audit:** the inherited native scorer also checks the aggregate alias margin; on all384 scientific baselines that extra condition agrees exactly with vocabulary-wide argmax correctness (zero discrepancies). Independent saved-tensor verification passed{t['n_checks']} checks, in addition to the frozen6752 score/journal checks and2520 production controls. Complete vectors, native full-depth traces, nonnative saved anchors and reconstructable archives passed their stated checks. Hash-only omitted arrays remain unrecoverable.",'', '![Descriptive prospective-panel summary](CONFIRMATION.png)','', '*Figure:* A shows complete-unit admission, B shows the open separating intervals (red means no separating interval), C uses the frozen mean-retention endpoint with valid-denominator counts, and D retains every raw native/intervened contrast. No panel is a new significance test.','', '**Practical conclusion:** this is a reproducible measurement finding worth building on. A correctness-filtered cross-model comparison can change sharply because it changes the linguistic sample being compared, even when both models are evaluated on the same selected subset. It does not yet reveal a distinct event-selection or linguistic-development mechanism, and direct selection precedent prevents a broad novelty claim. No further model inference follows.','']
